<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1859 0 R/Alt(Log-log plot of the electron plasma frequency in hertz against electron density per cubic metre. A straight line of slope one half rises from about 10 kilohertz at 10 to the 6 per cubic metre. Horizontal guides mark megahertz, gigahertz and terahertz. Five example plasmas lie on the line: H II region near 0.3 MHz, ionosphere near 9 MHz, solar corona near 0.3 GHz, Hall thruster near 9 GHz and tokamak core near 90 GHz.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[260]/Pg 17696 0 R>>
