2553 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 2554 0 R/Alt(Two log-log plots against r over the Debye length from 10 to the minus 5 to 8, for three strengths Lambda equal to 10 to the minus 4, minus 3 and minus 2. Left: the potential e Phi over k_B T_e. Close to the charge the exact Poisson-Boltzmann curves follow the bare Coulomb line; a marker shows where e Phi equals k_B T_e, at r about Lambda Debye lengths. Farther out, beyond about one Debye length, the exact and the dashed Debye-Hueckel curves coincide and fall exponentially. Right: the excess electron density n_e over n_0 minus one. Inside the marker the exact density rises exponentially far above the linearised one; outside, the two agree.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[26 27]/Pg 17709 0 R>>
endobj
